-- l4 run prints what l4 check reports of an @export (review of #779,
-- 2026-11-20): this one takes a function, which cannot be sent, and the file
-- is still evaluated. l4 deploy uploads it, past the local check, only to a
-- service that says it leaves such an export out (X-L4-Capabilities:
-- refused-exports; DEADWOOD), which then refuses the export; to any other
-- service it refuses the file before uploading.

@export Apply twice
GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`apply twice` MEANS f (f n)

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`double` m MEANS m * 2

#EVAL `apply twice` `double` 3
